{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Moses went.</b> He roused himself to this, as in וַיֵּלֶךְ אִישׁ מִבֵּית לֵוִי (Exodus 2:1), וַיֵּלֶךְ וַיַּעֲבֹד (Deuteronomy 17:3), and similar verses. That is, after he had completed the matter of covenant-making, he roused himself to comfort Israel regarding his death, so that they would not let the grief over his death mix with the joy of the covenant that was proper for them to show, demonstrating that they accepted the covenant with joy, after the manner of יִשְׂמַח יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּעֹשָׂיו (Psalms 149:2), as it says: וְזָבַחְתָּ שְׁלָמִים וְאָכַלְתָּ שָּׁם וְשָׂמַחְתָּ לִפְנֵי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ (Deuteronomy 27:7)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:44.056294267Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}